    "text": "To determine how many servings of peanut butter Toby should add to his toast to reach a total of 500 calories, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the calories from the bread. Toby has one piece of bread, and each piece has 100 calories.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Calories from bread} = 100 \\text{ calories}\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine the total calories needed from the peanut butter. Toby wants a total of 500 calories for breakfast.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Calories needed from peanut butter} = 500 \\text{ calories} - 100 \\text{ calories} = 400 \\text{ calories}\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the number of servings of peanut butter needed. Each serving of peanut butter has 200 calories.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of servings of peanut butter} = \\frac{400 \\text{ calories}}{200 \\text{ calories per serving}} = 2 \\text{ servings}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Toby should add \\(\\boxed{2}\\) servings of peanut butter.",
